;; fib.core.preds: true? false? NaN? infinite? (stdlib §4.3 rows; package FOLLOWUP-1, the cheap rows of the ADR 0023 list). Exports: true? false? NaN? infinite?.
;;  - `true?` and `false?` take a `bool` (Clojure's test the value itself: `(true? 1)` is false there; here a number is a type error, as everywhere); they are the identity and `not`.
;;  - `NaN?` and `infinite?` take an `f64`: NaN is the one value unequal to itself; infinite is either infinity, which `(- x x)` cannot tell from NaN, so they are compared.
(ns fib.core.preds)

(defun true? (x: bool) -> bool x)

(defun false? (x: bool) -> bool (not x))

(defun NaN? (x: f64) -> bool (!= x x))

(defun infinite? (x: f64) -> bool (or (= x (fdiv 1.0 0.0)) (= x (fdiv -1.0 0.0))))
